# rhwp change tracking for why-hwp: read it from HWP and write it to HWPX.
# Base: rhwp 981ce66b4 (v0.9.1) after the source edits in wasm/patch-rhwp.sh and
# wasm/patches/rhwp-layout.patch to rhwp-layout7.patch; apply this after
# rhwp-layout7.patch.
# Zero-context diff (apply with git apply --unidiff-zero). Every hunk inserts
# lines or changes lines of rhwp itself, away from the lines of the earlier
# patches.
#
# - DocInfo TRACK_CHANGE and TRACK_CHANGE_AUTHOR records are read into
#   DocInfo::track_changes and DocInfo::track_change_authors. The raw records
#   stay in extra_records, so an HWP save is unchanged.
# - HWPX gets hh:trackChanges and hh:trackChangeAuthors, the insertion (0x10)
#   and deletion (0x11) range tags become hp:insertBegin/End and
#   hp:deleteBegin/End, and a paragraph joined by a tracked deletion of the
#   break before it is written merged="1". Names, attributes, order, Id, TcId,
#   paraend and dates follow HWPX that Hancom Office wrote from the same HWP.
# - rhwp projects hidden tracked changes out of the IR it shows. An HWPX
#   export of a document that is still as loaded reads the file again without
#   that projection, so deleted text is kept inside its change marks.
# - Character (0x12) and paragraph (0x13) shape change range tags become
#   hp:run/@charTcId and hp:p/@paraTcId, as Hancom Office writes them.
